  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the primary uncertainty is whether a multimodal multiprofile pipeline outperforms simpler baselines and which component choices matter most. Config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is a well-balanced 'middle' configuration: it uses a proven RNA encoder (scvi_n200), a standard and efficient image encoder (resnet50), a lightweight aggregation (avgpool), and a simple weighted fusion. This tests the core hypothesis that combining RNA and image modalities with multiprofile aggregation is beneficial, while keeping training cost moderate (resnet50 + avgpool are both cheaper than ViT-L + transformer). If it performs strongly, subsequent experiments can isolate whether upgrading to transformer aggregation or ViT-L yields meaningful gains; if it underperforms, I can pivot to single-modality baselines. Expected relative cost: moderate (~40-50% of the most expensive configs like ViT-L + transformer), making it an efficient first probe that establishes a competitive baseline without consuming disproportionate GPU budget."
}

